<title>USA: Mellon Bank adopts new shareholder plan.</title>
<headline>Mellon Bank adopts new shareholder plan.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mellon Bank Corp said Tuesday it has adopted a new shareholder rights plan, setting an exercise price for the rights of $225.</p>
<p>Each right would entitle stockholders to buy $225 worth of stock at half price, the company said.</p>
<p>The plan would go into effect if an individual or group acquired 15 percent or more of the company's voting stock, it said.</p>
<p>In connection with the new plan, Mellon approved the redemption of rights issued under the 1989 rights agreement.</p>
</text>
